{"type":"text","timestamp":1794558749960,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf948e7ffenifDgTfvJ4O3eR","part":{"id":"prt_1d4095d550017dgT3qPPZTiqws","sessionID":"ses_e2bf948e7ffenifDgTfvJ4O3eR","messageID":"msg_1d409557100190EPI9DsCvu2xP","type":"text","text":"T042 complete.\n\n## Files written\n\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/devin.test.mjs` — new case `a damaged sessions database falls back to its transcript`: builds `devinSession({ root, projectDir })`, overwrites `fixture.dbPath` with `not a database`, expects `readSession` to return `ok` with `source.locatorKind` `transcript_file` and first item text `Read the file.`\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs` — `loadDevinSession` now falls back to `loadTranscript(sessionId, dataDirectory, options)` on a database open failure, a `null` projection, and a thrown query. The fallback returns the transcript when it is `ok` or `session_mismatch`, and `store_unreadable` otherwise. The `working_directory` mismatch still returns `session_mismatch` unchanged.\n\n## Verify\n\nTest first, before the implementation change:\n\n```\n✖ a damaged sessions database falls back to its transcript\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: Expected values to be strictly equal:\n  false !== true\nℹ tests 14\nℹ pass 13\nℹ fail 1\n```\n\nAfter the change, `node --test .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/devin.test.mjs`:\n\n```\n✔ a sessions database row and its chain resolve one session\n✔ a sessions database hit is preferred over a transcript with another id\n✔ a sessions row whose turns are not in the database falls through to its transcript\n✔ a damaged sessions database falls back to its transcript\n✔ a transcript outside the store is refused without reading it\n✔ a compacted session keeps the turns from before the compaction\n✔ a compacted session reports its continuation prompt as injected context\n✔ a session recorded in a folder below the named folder resolves\n✔ a sessions row for another working directory is a session_mismatch\n✔ a transcript that declares another session is a session_mismatch\n✔ an unknown id is a session_not_found when the database has other sessions\n✔ an absent transcript is a session_not_found when the store is present\n✔ a missing data directory is a store_unreadable\n✔ a sessions database linked outside the store is refused before it is opened\nℹ tests 14\nℹ pass 14\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\n`git status --short` for the two named paths shows only those two modifications.\n\n## Not done\n\nNothing outstanding. I did not tick the T042 checkbox in `tasks.md`, per instructions. I ran only the test file the task names, not the wider suite.","time":{"start":1794558745941,"end":1794558749960}}}
